{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Men of valor.</b> Who have strength and might to bear the burden, and will not fear them." "<b>God-fearers.</b> Who have no fear of man but only of HaShem." "<b>Haters of gain.</b> Rashi's comment: that they hate their own money in judgment, as in that which we say: any judge from whom money is taken in judgment is not a judge. They hate their money in judgment — how so? One of the litigants exaggerates to him: if you find me liable, I will burn your grain-stack and burn your vineyard; even so, he hates his money in judgment and does not regard it and does not refrain from finding him liable, and judges the judgment to its truth — that is what it means that they hate their money in judgment. But if he found the innocent one liable because of the other's exaggeration, the other party of this innocent one will extract money from him in judgment, so it turns out he is not a judge, for he did not judge a true judgment to its truth, as in that which we say: any judge from whom money is taken, etc. And thus we learn: he who judges the judgment, acquits the liable, or finds the innocent liable — what he did is done, and he pays from his own house, for he did not judge the judgment to its truth. <b>Haters of gain</b> — they hate their own money in judgment, all the more so that they hate the money of others and detest it to accept it as a bribe." "<b>Chiefs of thousands.</b> Rashi's comment: these were six hundred chiefs for the six hundred thousand, etc. And if you ask: if so, it turns out the judges of Israel were seventy thousand, and eight thousand, and six hundred chiefs — the count is too much! Therefore one must explain that all these chiefs were in addition to the sixty thousand of Israel and were not counted. And one may say that all these chiefs were perhaps elders over sixty years old, as we say in the chapter Yesh Nochalin, that those under twenty and over sixty were not counted. Another interpretation: the chiefs were from the count — the chief of the thousand from the thousand of Israel, the chief of the hundred from his hundred, and so for all of them."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {2 "הקב״ה resolved as HaShem; וכו׳ rendered as 'etc.' throughout.", 3 "שבעה רבוא ושמונה אלפים rendered literally as 'seventy thousand, and eight thousand'; בצרי להו שיעורא rendered as an Aramaic-inflected phrase meaning 'the count is too much.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:42.838545964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}